**Definition 1.3 (The fixed real frame and its sectors).** Put

$$
\begin{gathered}
D=\operatorname{diag}(1,i,i,i,1),\quad A=-iD^\dagger KD,\quad
O(t)=e^{tA}=D^\dagger U(t)D,\quad B=-A^2,\quad r=\sqrt{17},\\
\mu_\pm=(5\pm r)/2,\quad \omega_\pm=\sqrt{\mu_\pm},\quad
R_\pm=\frac{B(B-\mu_\mp I)}{\mu_\pm(\mu_\pm-\mu_\mp)},\quad
R_0=I-R_+-R_-=dd^T,\quad d=(e_2-e_5)/\sqrt2,\\
u_\pm=\frac{R_\pm e_N}{\sqrt{(1\pm1/r)/2}},\quad
W_\pm=AR_\pm/\omega_\pm,\quad v_\pm=W_\pm u_\pm,\\
G(\theta,\phi)=R_0+\cos\theta R_++\sin\theta W_+
                  +\cos\phi R_-+\sin\phi W_-,\quad
\mathsf J=\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1,1).
\end{gathered}
\tag{1.4}
$$

The spectral identities supplied by QMB Theorem 4.1 and
[QRC, Definition 3.1](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_QUANTUM_REAL_PORT_BOUNDARY_COORDINATES.md)
make $(d,u_+,v_+,u_-,v_-)$ an orthonormal real vector basis.
The sector ranks are $(n_0,n_+,n_-)=(1,2,2)$. In this basis
$\mathsf J=\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,-1,1,-1)$,
$\mathsf JG(\theta,\phi)\mathsf J=G(-\theta,-\phi)$, and
$O(t)=G(\omega_+t,\omega_-t)$. The irrational frequency ratio
has square $(21+5\sqrt{17})/4$; the actual nonnegative orbit has
the two-circle torus as its closure, as proved in
[QPC, Lemma 6.2](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_QUANTUM_PORT_COVARIANCE_AND_CERTIFIED_FRONTIER.md).
Write $\mathcal G$ for the group generated by this torus and
$\mathsf J$. These are mathematical design coordinates, not added
future controls. Transposes below are in this fixed real frame.

